<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/020D">Remark <span data-tag="020D">5.5.3.6</span>.</a> Let $\operatorname {h}\! \mathit{\operatorname{QCat}}$ denote the homotopy category of $\infty $-categories (Construction <a data-tag="01DR" href="/tag/01DR">4.5.1.1</a>), which we view as an $\operatorname {h}\! \mathit{\operatorname{Kan}}$-enriched category (see Remark <a data-tag="02L1" href="/tag/02L1">3.1.5.12</a>). Applying Proposition <a data-tag="00M4" href="/tag/00M4">2.4.6.9</a> and Corollary <a data-tag="02LP" href="/tag/02LP">4.6.8.20</a>, we obtain a canonical isomorphism of $\operatorname {h}\! \mathit{\operatorname{Kan}}$-enriched categories $\Phi : \operatorname {h}\! \mathit{\operatorname{QCat}} \xrightarrow {\sim } \operatorname {h}\! \mathit{\operatorname{\mathcal{QC}}}$, which is given on objects by the construction $\Phi (\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}) = \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ and on morphism spaces by the homotopy equivalences </p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  \operatorname{Hom}_{\operatorname{QCat}}( \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}, \operatorname{\mathcal{D}})_{\bullet } = \operatorname{Fun}(\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}, \operatorname{\mathcal{D}})^{\simeq } \rightarrow \operatorname{Hom}_{ \operatorname{\mathcal{QC}}}( \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}, \operatorname{\mathcal{D}}) \]
</div>
<p> of Remark <a data-tag="020F" href="/tag/020F">5.5.3.5</a>. </p>
</article>
